From 176afeb73442b51c486337648401231f7af34a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:09:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a headless recovery equivalent to the reset key

The racing state can strand a player where the rendered game expects
them to press R, and the headless bridge had no way to do that. Add
CRacing::HeadlessRecover(), which performs the same relocation
CReset::Loop does, to the nearest reset point behind the player or
half a course width and ten metres back up the hill when the course
defines none, re-initialises the controls, and advances the race
clock by the reset animation duration so recovering costs time as it
does on screen. The bridge exposes it as a "recover" command.

Signed-off-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
